{"name":"Dancing Dragonfly","hex":"#006658","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dancing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The activity of taking part in a dance.","A dance club in France."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of dance"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dancing"},{"term":"dragonfly","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An insect of the suborder Epiprocta or, more strictly, the infraorder Anisoptera, having four long transparent wings held perpendicular to a long body when perched."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dragonfly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dance","blocks":[{"text":"Dance is an art form, consisting of sequences of body movements with aesthetic and often symbolic value, either improvised or purposefully selected. Dance can be categorized and described by its choreography, by its repertoire of movements or by its historical period or place of origin. Dance is typically performed with musical accompaniment, and sometimes with the dancer simultaneously using a musical instrument themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Two_dancers.jpg/330px-Two_dancers.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dance"},{"title":"Dragonfly","blocks":[{"text":"A dragonfly is a flying insect belonging to the suborder Anisoptera of the order Odonata. About 3,000 living species of dragonflies are known. Most are tropical, with fewer species in temperate regions. Loss of wetland habitat threatens dragonfly populations around the world. Adult dragonflies are characterised by a pair of large, multifaceted, compound eyes, two pairs of strong, transparent wings, sometimes with coloured patches, and an elongated body. Many dragonflies have brilliant iridescent or metallic colours produced by structural coloration, making them conspicuous in flight. An adult dragonfly's 